ar, joint-output and funding/default reference checks pass; general simulation/result-query implementation remains pending. G2, G3, G6. |\n100:| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\ndocs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc:19:alternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\ndocs/design/fixtures/borrowing.acc:20:alternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:134:alternative allFixed { assume alpha == 1; }\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:135:alternative allFloating { assume alpha == 0; }\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:141:The parent model retains every $\\alpha\\in[0,1]$. The two named alternatives\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:142:are useful conditional views of that family, not a declaration that the\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:143:endpoints exhaust it. Requesting the parent family's exact bounds produces\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:145:conditional run of \\code{allFixed} supplies $\\alpha=1$. Requesting a weighted\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:207:evidence, author, creation time and scope. Child alternatives inherit all\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:212:Two independent alternatives may coexist, while two mutually exclusive readings\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:238:expressions, domains, constraints, alternatives, contracts, economic events,\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:267:preserve a justified conditional partition.\\\\\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:273:\\code{InsufficientSimulationState} & Add declared conditional assumptions or\ndocs/design/chapters/06-language.tex:280:a concrete unconditional result. The analyst can add a declared conditional\ndocs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md:55:and conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:573:    alternatives: tuple[AlternativeBinding, ...] = ()\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:581:                 alternatives: Sequence[AlternativeBinding] = ()):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:594:        object.__setattr__(self, \"alternatives\", tuple(alternatives))\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:600:        return _unique(self.alternatives, \"name\", name, \"MissingAlternativeMetadata\")\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:677:        alternatives = tuple(AlternativeBinding(name, \"synthetic-fixture-author\", reading.review_date,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:679:                             for name in (\"allFixed\", \"allFloating\"))\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:681:                   admissions=admissions, alternatives=alternatives,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:719:    unique(bindings.alternatives, \"name\", \"alternatives\")\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:813:    for alternative in bindings.alternatives:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:827:        \"symbols\", \"choices\", \"expressions\", \"constraints\", \"assumptions\", \"alternatives\",\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:867:        self.alternatives: dict[str, AlternativeDecl] = {}\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:952:                self.alternatives[decl.name] = decl\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:970:        if len(self.alternatives) < 1:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1365:        # Contract, alternatives, and scenario expressions.\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1386:        for alt in self.alternatives.values():\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1398:                self.fail(\"MissingAlternativeCondition\", \"named alternatives require a Boolean condition\", alt.name)\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1399:            self.ir[\"alternatives\"].append({\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1403:                \"constraints\": alt_constraints, \"choice_group\": None,\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1463:            \"alternatives\": alt_ids, \"feasibility\": \"Unknown\", \"coverage\": \"PartialSearch\",\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1480:        self.ir[\"alternatives\"].sort(key=lambda r: r[\"id\"])\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1938:            if row[\"scope\"] not in model_ids | scope_ids and row[\"scope\"] not in {a[\"id\"] for a in ir[\"alternatives\"]} and row[\"scope\"] not in {c[\"id\"] for c in ir[\"contracts\"]} and row[\"scope\"] not in {s[\"id\"] for s in ir[\"scenarios\"]}:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1997:        alternatives = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"alternatives\"]}\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:1998:        for row in ir[\"alternatives\"]:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2001:            meta = next((a for a in bindings.alternatives if a.name == row[\"id\"]), None)\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2039:            if set(row[\"symbols\"]) != {s[\"id\"] for s in ir[\"symbols\"]} or set(row[\"alternatives\"]) != set(alternatives):\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2040:                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"FamilyMembership\", \"family must retain all shared symbols and alternatives\", row[\"id\"]))\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2096:                \"symbols\", \"contracts\", \"alternatives\", \"scenarios\", \"reportMappings\") for r in ir[k]}\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2108:    alternatives = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"alternatives\"]}\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2109:    if not alternatives:\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2110:        raise _diag(\"ProfileCardinality\", \"at least one alternative is required\", \"alternatives\")\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2113:        if row[\"scope\"] not in set(alternatives) | {scope[\"id\"]} or row[\"kind\"] != \"assumption\":\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2116:    for alt in alternatives.values():\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2134:        key = (\"alternative\" if row[\"scope\"] in alternatives else\nscripts/core0_ir_v1.py:2205:    # source context, package locks, assumptions, alternatives and bindings.\n68:semantic checker validate these specific bindings; general registry resolution\n102:stress driver as assumptions. The integer contract-slot limit has its own\n112:`simpleInterest(principal,rate,fraction)` explicitly. Integer counts stay integer.\n120:precision is a domain, not a tolerance argument. Unknown rounding convention\n124:available; `rounding_rule` identifies the declared convention or is null for\n125:an unrounded mathematical symbol. The SourceSpan retains the original text.\n132:an unknown rounding convention.\n144:| roundMoney | Money<C>, Int, String -> Money<C>; only half_even supported in DemoDebt; rounding at posting boundary, rational ties exact |\n159:timing/calendar resolution, allowed choices, bounds, and forbidden/unsupported\n179:Money quantisation either occurs after continuous analysis or uses integer\n180:minor-unit variables with a separately declared bounded integer solver. Integer\n182:Unknown-by-unknown products, symbolic discount rates/exponents, arbitrary\n183:functions and unbounded integer search return UnsupportedFragment/Unknown.\n185:linear even when D is rounded. A fixed constraint F/D >= a with known a and\n190:attainment flags, proof/certificate reference, rounding stage and scope. Strict\n235:corrections replace evidence views; likelihoods update probability models;\n240:event probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\n241:weights exactly. Zero probability yields UndefinedConditioning, not equal\n260:NumericalFailure, SolverUnknown, Cancelled. Default retains the legal obligations\n283:hashes normalised IR, assumptions, rule/calculator locks and resolution contract,\n299:rational (integer+1/2)/2^64. Branch enumeration order is absent. Coupling groups\n328:| reconstruct | IR, ModelScope, view, solver_lock, budgets | HistoryFamily and cell coverage, witnesses/conflicts/unknowns |\n331:| bound | formula, query expression, domain, quantisation mode, solver/budget | certified bound/attainment or explicit Unknown/Unbounded |\n353:numerical metadata, never historical probabilities. These are adapter designs\n354:grounded in archived interfaces. Only Z3 is exercised by the reference checks.\n377:  interval additionally needs the declared rounding convention; scale alone\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
