{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '220,245p' docs/design/spec/core-contract.md\nsed -n '46,66p' docs/design/spec/core0-lowering-profile-v1.md\nsed -n '1997,2010p' scripts/core0_ir_v1.py\nsed -n '98,102p' docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md\nrg -n 'alternative|allFixed|allFloating|family|compile|load_' tests/test_accounting_p03.py\"","aggregated_output":"bytes. Correction creates a new reading linked to the old one; replacing an\naccepted reading requires a supersession action. An unresolved contradiction\nsets conflict, even if each extraction was accepted. No LLM confidence becomes\na hypothesis weight. Derived formulas, mappings, measurements and runs record\ndependency IDs; a changed decision makes their descendants stale for new\nviews. Historic frozen runs remain replayable, labelled with their old view.\n\n## Uncertainty, scenarios and results\n\nUncertainty kinds are ExtractionReading, HistoricalFact, AccountingElection,\nMeasurementEstimate, BehaviourPolicy and FutureInnovation. Each has scope,\ndomain, evidence, dependencies and admission rule. An election needs a dated\npermitted treatment and evidence of eligibility; a balanced but prohibited\ntreatment is UnsupportedTreatment. Estimates need a method/date/inputs; future\ninnovations need a joint law and measure. New observations constrain facts;\ncorrections replace evidence views; likelihoods update probability models;\nhypothetical stresses alone do none of those.\n\nExogenousStress supplies named driver paths without updating historical weights.\nObservationalConditioning supplies observed events, a joint model and positive\nevent probability/likelihood; finite enumeration computes normalised joint\nweights exactly. Zero probability yields UndefinedConditioning, not equal\nweights. Continuous density conditioning requires an explicit conditional\nmodel/regular conditional distribution adapter. StructuralIntervention replaces\nspecified equations in a named acyclic structural model, retaining exogenous\nnoise; absence of that model yields UnsupportedScenario. Risk-neutral pricing\n\n## Supported language and bindings\n\nThe profile has one module, DemoDebt@1 import, source, entity, USD book, exact\ninstant debt observation, admitted Real interval symbol, opening, DebtMix\ncontract, constant annual-rate stress and package report. Its four account names\nare Cash, Debt, InterestExpense and Retained, with Asset, Liability, Expense and\nEquity roles respectively: the package report actually names these accounts.\nOther declaration names may vary. There may be multiple lets, Boolean constraints\nand conditional alternatives, with multiple assumptions in each alternative.\nGlobal constraints constrain the parent family; alternative constraints stay in\ntheir respective branches and are not conjoined in the parent. No branch is\nselected or solved.\n\nBindings explicitly supply a digest-locked local package, synthetic reading and\nacceptance action, information/system cutoffs, opening balances, perimeter,\nsymbol admission, assumption periods/origins, and alternative authorship. Binding\nrecords remain separate from package definitions. Every acceptance must explicitly\nsay Accept; no declaration creates acceptance. Package loading is restricted to\nthe retained DemoDebt file and checks its fixed version, digest, exports and\napplicability. Paths escaping the repository and overrides are errors. The\n        alternatives = {r[\"id\"]: r for r in ir[\"alternatives\"]}\n        for row in ir[\"alternatives\"]:\n            if row[\"parent\"] not in {r[\"id\"] for r in ir[\"historyFamilies\"]} or row[\"scope\"] not in scope_ids:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"AlternativeScope\", \"alternative parent or scope is unknown\", row[\"id\"]))\n            meta = next((a for a in bindings.alternatives if a.name == row[\"id\"]), None)\n            if meta is None or row[\"author\"] != meta.author or row[\"created_at\"] != meta.created_at or row[\"reason\"] != meta.reason:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"AlternativeMetadata\", \"alternative metadata differs from binding\", row[\"id\"]))\n            if not row[\"constraints\"]:\n                raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"MissingAlternativeCondition\", \"alternative requires at least one condition\", row[\"id\"]))\n            for cid in row[\"constraints\"]:\n                c = next((x for x in ir[\"constraints\"] if x[\"id\"] == cid), None)\n                if c is None or c[\"scope\"] != row[\"id\"] or checker.expr(c[\"expression\"])[0] != \"Bool\":\n                    raise _Failure(Diagnostic(\"AlternativeScope\", \"alternative condition is not scoped to its branch\", row[\"id\"]))\n        for row in ir[\"states\"]:\n| MC24 | Specify the core language and IR completely enough for compatible independent implementations. U3, D. | Provide complete grammar/lexical rules, AST/IR schemas, types, context rules, built-ins, errors, package interfaces and source-to-IR-to-result fixtures, including the demonstration package. | Core 0 grammar, closed structural IR, built-ins, arities, context/domain rules and complete debt dependency package supplied. Authored expected IR and selected expression-to-result checks pass. A frozen 17-export registry and bounded debt static validator now pass positive and schema-valid negative cases. General compilation, package loading, remaining semantic conformance and independent implementability assessment remain open. G2, G12, G15. |\n| MC25 | Specify APIs, adapters, storage, versioning, identity and deterministic recovery. U3, P, D. | Define complete arguments/results, state ownership, migration semantics, evidence/model/run identity, event idempotency, random-stream allocation and replay requirements with examples. | Specified APIs, ownership, canonical identity, migration/replay and stream keying in Ch. 10/Core 0; concrete adapter exchanges included. Reference identity, replay/conflict, stream and bounded frozen-export integrity checks pass; transactional storage, migrations and non-Z3 adapters remain unimplemented. G2, G9, G18. |\n| MC26 | Specify supported numerical/solver operations and their limits. U3, P, D. | Define formula fragments, reformulations, exact/approximate monetary treatment, rounding, strict-domain bounds, infeasibility/conflict evidence, timeout and resource behaviour. | Specified rational-linear/finite-choice scope, amount reformulation, quantisation distinctions and typed unknowns in Ch. 6/Core 0. Z3 checks 4.975 attained and 7.035 unattained and concrete histories. Nonlinear solvers and a production rounding/optimization layer remain pending. G3, G10. |\n| MC27 | Specify analyst/LLM review and correction as a traceable local workflow. U1, U3, D. | Define proposal, acceptance, alternative, rejection and supersession actions, with evidence requirements, consistency checks and derived-result invalidation; show an actual conflict-resolution example. | Specified Propose/Accept/AcceptAlternative/Reject/Supersede actions, examples and dependency invalidation in Ch. 10/Core 0. The transitive invalidation oracle passes; a complete analyst UI/workflow and human adjudication remain pending. G2, G17. |\n| MC28 | Connect the full design through complete synthetic and real disclosure cases. U1, U2, U3, D. | Supply a known-history synthetic company and a named annual/interim real package across multiple dates; trace representative notes through records, constraints, alternatives and all affected future statements. Add structural finance/sector cases before fixing the core types. | Reference cases delivered in Ch. 2: complete synthetic Northstar history/revision/forecast and named Apple annual/interim inventory, notes and conditional stress. Ch. 9 supplies sector/finance structures. Real-company full semantic closure and independent case annotation remain open; no complete Apple forecast is claimed. G4, G